Subject: [PATCH] Fritchii v5: framebuffers indexed by image view, drift shortcut in JoinImages' overlap walk (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_FBINDEX / EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DRIFT, off by default)

Port of Frizti/Fritchii d69ecefe34 (author Frizti, with Claude Opus 5.5; fable_answer_12 2E),
without its rt_stats lines (fc40c591e9 is not in this tree).

- EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_FBINDEX=1: GetFramebufferId files each new framebuffer under its views
  (framebuffers_by_view) and its key (framebuffer_keys); RemoveFramebuffers takes a deleted image's
  framebuffers from the index instead of scanning the whole framebuffer map, which grows by one
  entry per drifted render target per frame until the collector deletes them. A null view in the
  list still takes the full scan (which now also unindexes). Same framebuffers removed either way:
  every key holding one of the views; ASSERTs on the key lookup and on framebuffers.erase(key)==1.
  The only users of the map are GetFramebufferId's try_emplace and RemoveFramebuffers (checked).
- EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DRIFT=1: a single-level, single-layer 2D image overlapping another such image
  (same layer stride) at a non-zero offset under one layer, its size and the other's size is filed
  as a bad overlap at once. That offset is no mip or layer base of either image (TryFindBase /
  ResolveOverlapLeft/Right2D need a mip offset of 0 for one level), so ResolveOverlap and both
  IsSubresource checks would return nothing: same outcome, less CPU. Separate switch so the
  equivalence can be A/B'd on its own.

Checks (fritchii-fbindex_checks.sh, log fritchii-fbindex.checks.log): git apply --check on
$R/Eglantine; 6 anchor skips before and after (same); only the generated texture_cache.h copy
differs; -fsyntax-only of vk_texture_cache_base.cpp (Vulkan instantiation), vk_texture_cache_cost,
vulkan_rasterizer, gl_texture_cache_base, texture_cache.cpp: rc=0; injected static_assert in
texture_cache_base.h and 4 injected calls in the new code (index, unindex, indexed removal, drift
shortcut) all reported by the Vulkan instantiation. Stacks with the other fritchii-*.diff in any order.

Expected effect: less back-thread CPU in collector bursts (each delete scanned the whole map) and in
JoinImages for drifted targets; no memory cost (two small maps). Risk: low; a desync shows as an
ASSERT in the log.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 968ae0f..715f414 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -71,6 +71,24 @@ namespace VideoCommon {
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_FBINDEX=1 (off unless set; Fritchii d69ecefe34, fable_answer_12 2E): the
+/// framebuffers are indexed by their image views, so RemoveFramebuffers takes a deleted image's
+/// framebuffers from the index instead of scanning the whole framebuffer map (one entry per
+/// drifted render target a frame until the collector deletes them). Same framebuffers removed.
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool FritchiiFramebufferIndex() {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_FBINDEX");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
+/// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DRIFT=1 (off unless set; Fritchii d69ecefe34): JoinImages files a single-level,
+/// single-layer 2D image that overlaps another such image at an offset under one layer (and not
+/// 0) as a bad overlap at once: that offset is no mip or layer base of either image, so
+/// ResolveOverlap and both IsSubresource checks would fail anyway.
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool FritchiiDriftShortcut() {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DRIFT");
+    return enabled;
+}
